# Child Theme Only

All customizations for this site go in `sober-child` only.

## Do

- Edit files under `wp-content/themes/sober-child/`
- Override parent templates by copying them into the child theme (same relative path)
- Override WooCommerce templates via `sober-child/woocommerce/...`
- Override WPBakery / VC templates via `sober-child/vc_templates/...`
- Add hooks, enqueues, and filters in `sober-child/functions.php` (or includes loaded from there)
- Add CSS/JS under `sober-child/src/` (scss/js), compile to `assets/`, enqueue from the child
## Do not

- Edit `wp-content/themes/sober/` (parent theme)
- Edit `wp-content/plugins/` (including `js_composer`, `woocommerce`, `sober-addons`)
- Edit WordPress core
- Patch parent files "temporarily" — use child overrides or hooks instead

## Override pattern

1. Find the template/hook in the parent theme or plugin (read-only).
2. Implement the change in `sober-child` via template copy, hook, or enqueue.
3. Prefer hooks/filters over copying large templates when possible.

If a change seems to require editing the parent or a plugin, stop and explain the child-theme approach instead.
